# Kill ports when done

When a task is finished (or before ending the turn after starting a local server), free the ports you used.

- Stop any Next.js / Node / Vite / other local servers started in the session.
- Kill processes holding common project ports (especially `3000`, and any other ports this session opened).
- Prefer killing by port/PID for this project rather than leaving `npm run dev` running.
- Do this by default at the end of the task. The user should not have to ask.
- Do not leave background servers running after you are done unless the user explicitly asked to keep them up.
